From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:42:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/43] app-list: exit when the Wayland connection has a
 protocol error

After a protocol error, dispatch keeps returning Ok without blocking, so
the Wayland thread spun. Log the error once and exit the process: ending
only the thread would leave an empty taskbar, since the app list never
starts its handler again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BLrpLktNVQBZowKMy1ebh2

diff --git a/cosmic-app-list/src/wayland_handler.rs b/cosmic-app-list/src/wayland_handler.rs
index 31fb84ea..ba8eea8a 100644
--- a/cosmic-app-list/src/wayland_handler.rs
+++ b/cosmic-app-list/src/wayland_handler.rs
@@ -708,6 +708,13 @@ pub(crate) fn wayland_handler(
             break;
         }
         event_loop.dispatch(None, &mut app_data).unwrap();
+        // A dead connection makes dispatch return Ok without blocking, so it would spin. Exit
+        // instead of ending the thread: the app list never restarts its handler, and the panel
+        // restarts the applet.
+        if let Some(err) = app_data.conn.protocol_error() {
+            tracing::error!("Wayland connection closed by a protocol error: {err}");
+            std::process::exit(1);
+        }
     }
 }
 
